+  /** Test case for
+   * <a href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CALCITE-7051">[CALCITE-7051]
+   * JOIN with USING does not match the appropriate columns when caseSensitive is false</a>:
+   * a NATURAL JOIN's common column expands to a COALESCE of the two sides, the same way a
+   * USING column does. Before the fix, {@code expandExprFromJoin} special-cased
+   * {@code JoinConditionType.USING} and returned every NATURAL JOIN column unexpanded, so
+   * {@code DEPTNO} resolved as an ambiguous, unqualified reference to both {@code EMP.DEPTNO}
+   * and {@code DEPT.DEPTNO} regardless of case sensitivity. */
+  @Test void testNaturalJoinCommonColumnIsExpandedToCoalesce() {
